Independent implementation based on the Jsonnet language specification,
language reference and standard-library contracts at https://jsonnet.org/.

Development-only reference: Google Jsonnet v0.21.0
https://github.com/google/jsonnet
Copyright Google Inc.; Apache License 2.0.
Pinned commit: bbb38f1020be1f5aed560928fb839b2c448cefb4.
No upstream interpreter is bundled or linked.
The committed differential inputs and example fixtures are original project
material, distributed under this project's Apache-2.0 license. The reference
checkout retains its own LICENSE and third-party notices outside this package.
tools/upstream-language.mbtx executes selected upstream Apache-2.0 test files
and extracts individual formatting assertions into temporary test artifacts.
These upstream assertions remain Google copyright and are not bundled in the
published package. See the pinned reference checkout for their license headers.

Functional implementation reference: Google go-jsonnet v0.21.0
https://github.com/google/go-jsonnet
Copyright Google Inc.; Apache License 2.0.
Pinned commit: 67968688d9952f50662e979fab1bef889d0d3e57.
The Go interpreter is used only for development-time behavioral comparisons;
its implementation is not bundled or linked into this package.

stdlib_source.mbt embeds the Jsonnet standard-library source from the pinned
go-jsonnet astgen/stdast.go above. Copyright Google Inc.; Apache License 2.0
(see LICENSE and the original header embedded in stdlib_source.mbt).
tools/embed-stdlib.mbtx verifies the reference revision and extracts the source;
stdlib_layer.mbt selects supported definitions. This Jsonnet source is evaluated
by MoonJsonnet's own MoonBit interpreter; no Go interpreter is required at runtime.

format_power.mbt adapts the fractional base-10 evaluation path from the Go
standard library, Go 1.24.0 src/math/pow.go:
https://github.com/golang/go/blob/go1.24.0/src/math/pow.go
Copyright 2009 The Go Authors. All rights reserved.
It is distributed under the BSD 3-Clause terms in licenses/GO-BSD-3-Clause.txt.
This is separate from the development-only go-jsonnet interpreter reference.

reference_math.mbt and reference_trig.mbt adapt Go 1.24.0 src/math/atan.go,
atan2.go, asin.go, exp.go, exp_arm64.s, pow.go, sin.go, tan.go, and trig_reduce.go:
https://github.com/golang/go/tree/go1.24.0/src/math
Copyright 2009, 2011, 2017, 2018 The Go Authors. All rights reserved.
BSD 3-Clause terms: licenses/GO-BSD-3-Clause.txt. Inherited Cephes and Sun
Microsystems notices are retained in licenses/GO-MATH-NOTICES.txt.

MoonBit core is provided by the user's toolchain, not vendored here. Automation
scripts use moonbitlang/async (Apache-2.0), resolved by Moon script mode; it is not
a library runtime dependency. Official examples informed the package layout:
https://github.com/moonbitlang/async/tree/main/examples
